WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.290
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:10.559
This new learning-based method is capable
of generating new videos, creating lava from

00:00:10.559 --> 00:00:16.940
water, enhancing your dance videos, adding
new players to a football game, and more.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:19.820
This one will feel like it can do absolutely
anything!

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:22.760
For instance, have a look at these videos.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:28.630
Believe it or not, some of these were generated
by an AI from this new paper.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:33.710
Let’s try to find out together which ones
are real, and which are generated.

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:39.640
Now before we start, many of the results that
you will see here will be flawed, but I promise

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:42.460
that there will be some gems in there too.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:44.730
This one doesn’t make too much sense.

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:45.730
One down.

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:50.320
Two, the bus appears to be changing length
from time to time.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:55.040
Three, the bus pops out of existence.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:03.670
Four…wait…this actually looks pretty good…until
we find out that someone is about to get rear-ended.

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:05.549
This leaves us with two examples.

00:01:05.549 --> 00:01:08.850
Are they real, or are they fakes?

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:13.230
Now, please stop the video and let me know
in the comments.

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:16.310
So, this one is real footage.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:18.530
Okay, what about this guy?

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:24.200
Well, get this…this one is actually one
of the generated ones.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.710
Just this one was real.

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:28.820
And this is what this new technique is capable
of.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:33.939
We give it a sample video, and it reimagines
variations of it.

00:01:33.939 --> 00:01:40.500
Of course, the results are hit or miss, for
instance, here, people and cars just pop in

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:44.950
and out of existence, but if we try it on
the billiard balls.

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:48.000
Wow, now this is something.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:53.400
Look at how well it preserved the specular
highlights, and also, the shadows move with

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:56.150
the balls in the synthetic variations too.

00:01:56.150 --> 00:02:01.580
Once again, the results are generally quite
hit or miss, but if we look through a few

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:04.050
results, we often find some gems out there.

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:07.439
But this is nothing compared to what is to
come.

00:02:07.439 --> 00:02:13.690
Let’s call this first feature video synthesis,
and we have 4 more really cool applications

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:17.989
with somewhat flawed, but sometimes amazing
results.

00:02:17.989 --> 00:02:22.480
Now, check this out, here comes number two,
video analogies.

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:29.940
This makes it possible for us to mix two videos
that depict things that follow a similar logic.

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:37.180
For instance, here, only four of these sixteen
videos are real, the rest are all generated.

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:41.239
Now, here comes feature number three - time
retargeting.

00:02:41.239 --> 00:02:45.550
For instance, we can lengthen or shorten videos.

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:51.770
Well, that sounds simple enough, no need for
an AI for that…but here is the key!

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:56.300
This does not mean just adding new frames
to the end of the video.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:57.300
Look!

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:58.730
They are different.

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:03.150
Yes, the entirety of the video is getting
redesigned here.

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:08.620
We can use this to lengthen these videos without
really adding new content to it.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:10.310
Absolutely amazing.

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:13.239
We can also use it to shorten a video.

00:03:13.239 --> 00:03:18.130
Now, of course, once again, this doesn’t
mean that it just chops off the end of the

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:19.130
video.

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:20.130
No-no!

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:22.970
It means something much more challenging.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:23.970
Look!

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:29.360
It makes sure that all of your killer moves
make it into the video, but, in a shorter

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:30.459
amount of time.

00:03:30.459 --> 00:03:33.830
It makes the video tighter if you will.

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:35.290
Amazing feature number 4.

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:37.019
Sketch to video.

00:03:37.019 --> 00:03:44.250
Here, we can take an input video, add a crude
drawing, and the video will follow this drawing.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:50.530
The result is, of course, not perfect, but,
in return, this can handle many number to

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.610
number transitions.

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:54.959
And now, feature number five.

00:03:54.959 --> 00:03:57.450
Video inpainting on steroids.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:03.810
Previous techniques can help us delete part
of an image, or even a video, and generate

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:08.069
data in these holes that make sense given
their surroundings.

00:04:08.069 --> 00:04:11.840
But this, this one does something way better!

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:18.069
Look, we can cut out different parts of a
video, and mark the missing region with a

00:04:18.069 --> 00:04:20.199
color, and then, what happens?

00:04:20.199 --> 00:04:21.459
Oh yes!

00:04:21.459 --> 00:04:26.879
The blue regions will contain a player from
the blue team, the white region a player from

00:04:26.879 --> 00:04:32.559
the white team, or, if we wish to get someone
out of the way, we can do that too.

00:04:32.559 --> 00:04:34.949
Just mark them green.

00:04:34.949 --> 00:04:40.729
Here, the white regions will be inpainted
with clouds, and the blues with birds.

00:04:40.729 --> 00:04:41.729
Loving it.

00:04:41.729 --> 00:04:47.229
But wait a second, we noted that there are
already good techniques out there for image

00:04:47.229 --> 00:04:48.229
inpainting.

00:04:48.229 --> 00:04:52.270
There are also good techniques for video time
retargeting.

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:54.969
So, what is so interesting here?

00:04:54.969 --> 00:04:56.669
Well, two things.

00:04:56.669 --> 00:05:02.069
One, here all of these things are being done
with just one technique.

00:05:02.069 --> 00:05:07.050
Normally, we would need a collection of different
methods to perform all of these.

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:09.580
But here, just one AI.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:14.740
Two, now hold on to your papers, and look
at this!

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:15.740
Whoa.

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:19.270
Previous techniques take forever to generate
these results.

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:26.900
144p means an extremely crude, pixelated image,
and even then, they take from hours…to,

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:28.460
my goodness.

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:29.490
Even days.

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:31.509
So, what about this new one?

00:05:31.509 --> 00:05:37.610
It can generate much higher resolution images,
and, in a matter of minutes.

00:05:37.610 --> 00:05:40.870
That is an incredible leap in just one paper.

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:44.080
Now, clearly, most of these results aren’t
perfect.

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:47.979
I would argue that they are not even close
to perfect.

00:05:47.979 --> 00:05:51.080
But some of them already show a lot of promise.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:57.099
And, as always, dear Fellow Scholars, do not
forget to apply the First Law of Papers.

00:05:57.099 --> 00:05:59.939
Which says, do not look at where we are.

00:05:59.939 --> 00:06:03.389
Look at where we will be two more papers down
the line.

00:06:03.389 --> 00:06:09.979
And two more papers down the line, I am sure
that not two, but five, or maybe even six

00:06:09.979 --> 00:06:35.419
out of these six videos will look significantly

00:06:35.419 --> 00:06:46.869
more real.

00:06:46.869 --> 00:06:58.319
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

